    "hardware_bias_mechanism_explanation": "Layer 1 (Conv1, 3->8, 3x3) executes inside the HLS Streaming 2D Convolution Engine using ap_fixed<16,8> (Q8.8 signed fixed-point), where CONV1_BIAS[k] is added directly to each filter's 3x3x3 accumulator at every pixel and timestep before the V_th=1.0 LIF check. Layer 2 (Conv2, 8->16, 3x3) executes in HLS Phase 2a/2/3 using 8-bit signed integer weights (CONV2_WEIGHTS), 16-bit signed integer biases (CONV2_BIAS[16] = round(4 * SCALE2 * b2_f) added once per timestep in Phase 2a), and 16-bit signed membrane potentials (cnn_l2_v_mem[16][16][16]). Layer 3 (Classifier, 1024->10) executes on RTL Core Group 4, which receives Layer 2 spike events from Relay Core Groups 0..3 (4x256=1,024 neurons) and uses Event-Driven Synaptic Bias Folding: W3_folded[c, j] = W3_f[c, j] + alpha * b3_f[c].",
